# Admin TMS iRFQ (locked spec)

Create TMS iRFQ uses the **TMS-integration server bot** (`TMS_BOT_EMAIL` / `TMS_BOT_PASSWORD`). Do not require the Sales portal user to sign in with a TMS password to create.

After a successful create, **MUST**:

1. Persist `tmsId`, `tmsDocumentNo`, and details `tmsUrl` on that marketplace RFQ (`accepted` or `quoted`).
2. Replace **Create TMS iRFQ** with **Open [iRFQ document no.]** (example: `Open iRFQ-26000759-01`). Never keep Create once `tmsDocumentNo` exists.
3. The Open control is a link to **that iRFQ details page**: `{TMS_BASE_URL}/inbound/inbound-rfq/{tmsId}` — not the inbound list (`?current=1&pageSize=20`).

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — stays Create after success, or opens the list
<button>Create TMS iRFQ</button>
<a href="https://uat-tms-v2.mattex.com.hk/inbound/inbound-rfq?current=1&pageSize=20">Open TMS</a>

// ✅ GOOD
<a href="https://uat-tms-v2.mattex.com.hk/inbound/inbound-rfq/2879">Open iRFQ-26000759-01</a>
```
